> # Suggested module structure
> 
> Here’s a clean filesystem layout for this:
> 
> ```text
> memory/
>     __init__.py
>     models.py
>     protocols.py
>     long_term.py
>     conversation.py
>     store_sqlalchemy.py
>     store_inmemory.py
>     index_whoosh.py
>     index_null.py
>     model_openai.py
>     model_mock.py
>     fixtures.py
> tests/
>     test_conversation_memory.py
>     test_long_term_memory.py
>     test_memory_integration.py
> ```
> 
> ---
> 
> # `models.py`
> 
> This would hold the dataclasses I sketched earlier:
> 
> - `Message`
> - `ConversationTranscript`
> - `MemoryRecord`
> - `UserProfile`
> - `TaskRecord`
> - `RetrievedMemoryBundle`
> - `ConversationState`
> - `PostProcessResult`
> 
> You already have those prototypes above.
> 
> ---
> 
> # `protocols.py`
> 
> This would hold:
> 
> - `MemoryStore`
> - `MemoryIndex`
> - `MemoryModel`
> 
> This is important because it keeps all core orchestration code decoupled from SQLAlchemy/Whoosh/OpenAI.
> 
> ---
