**user**:
> Can you define the three unit tests you propose?
**assistant**:
> Yes. I’d propose **three core unit tests** first, covering:
> 
> 1. **ConversationMemory updates and emits a prompt block**
> 2. **LongTermMemory post-process stores extracted memories and updates profile**
> 3. **Multi-user isolation / retrieval correctness**
> 
> These give you strong coverage of the essential behavior without dragging in real DBs or real model calls.
> 
> ---
> 
> # 1. `test_conversation_memory_updates_and_returns_prompt_block`
> 
> ## Purpose
> Verify that `ConversationMemory.update_with_turn(...)`:
> 
> - appends assistant/user messages correctly
> - updates conversation state
> - calls retrieval through `LongTermMemory`
> - returns a nonempty prompt block containing relevant memory
> 
> This tests the **within-conversation loop**.
> 
> ## Why it matters
> This is the heart of the “agent feels persistent during a conversation” behavior.
> 
> ## Test setup
> Use:
> - `InMemoryStore`
> - `MockMemoryModel`
> - `SimpleTextMemoryIndex`
> 
> Seed one prior memory for the user, such as:
> - fact: “Uses Python”
> - preference: “Prefers concise answers”
> 
> Then create a `ConversationMemory` and simulate a turn.
> 
> ## Example test
> 
> ```python
> def test_conversation_memory_updates_and_returns_prompt_block():
>     store = InMemoryStore()
>     model = MockMemoryModel()
>     index = SimpleTextMemoryIndex(store)
>     ltm = LongTermMemory(store=store, model=model, index=index)
> 
>     user_id = "alice"
>     ltm.initialize_user(user_id)
> 
>     ltm.remember(
>         MemoryRecord(
>             memory_id="",
>             user_id=user_id,
>             kind="fact",
>             content="Uses Python for AI systems",
>             summary="Uses Python for AI systems",
>             created_at=datetime.utcnow(),
>             source="test",
>             importance=0.9,
>             confidence=1.0,
>             tags=["python"],
>         )
>     )
> 
>     convo = ltm.start_conversation(
>         user_id=user_id,
>         conversation_id="conv-1",
>         initial_query="Help me design a Python memory system",
>     )
> 
>     block = convo.update_with_turn(
>         assistant_response="What kind of memory do you want?",
>         user_response="I want long-term memory for my Python assistant.",
>     )
> 
>     assert "Relevant memory:" in block
>     assert "Uses Python for AI systems" in block
> 
>     state = convo.get_state()
>     assert state.running_summary
>     assert any("Python assistant" in p or "Python" in p for p in state.important_points)
> ```
> 
> ## What it validates
> - prompt block generation works
> - retrieval is wired in
> - transcript and state update correctly
> 
> ---
> 
> # 2. `test_post_process_conversation_stores_memories_and_updates_profile`
> 
> ## Purpose
> Verify that `LongTermMemory.post_process_conversation(...)`:
> 
> - saves the conversation
> - creates a conversation summary memory
> - extracts candidate memories from the transcript
> - stores them
> - updates the user profile
> 
> This tests the **between-conversations persistence pipeline**.
> 
> ## Why it matters
> This is the core long-term memory behavior.
> 
> ## Test setup
> Use:
> - `InMemoryStore`
> - `MockMemoryModel`
> - optionally `NullMemoryIndex` or `SimpleTextMemoryIndex`
> 
> Create a transcript with user messages like:
> - `remember: I use Python`
> - `preference: concise answers`
> - `task: build a memory manager`
> 
> Then call `post_process_conversation`.
> 
> ## Example test
> 
> ```python
> def test_post_process_conversation_stores_memories_and_updates_profile():
>     store = InMemoryStore()
>     model = MockMemoryModel()
>     index = SimpleTextMemoryIndex(store)
>     ltm = LongTermMemory(store=store, model=model, index=index)
> 
>     user_id = "bob"
>     transcript = ConversationTranscript(
>         conversation_id="conv-2",
>         user_id=user_id,
>         started_at=datetime.utcnow(),
>         ended_at=datetime.utcnow(),
>         messages=[
>             Message(role="user", content="remember: I use Python", created_at=datetime.utcnow()),
>             Message(role="user", content="preference: concise answers", created_at=datetime.utcnow()),
>             Message(role="user", content="task: build a memory manager", created_at=datetime.utcnow()),
>         ],
>     )
> 
>     result = ltm.post_process_conversation(transcript)
> 
>     assert result.stored_memory_ids
>     assert result.updated_profile is True
> 
>     memories = ltm.list_user_memories(user_id)
>     assert any(m.kind == "conversation_summary" for m in memories)
>     assert any(m.kind == "fact" and m.content == "I use Python" for m in memories)
>     assert any(m.kind == "preference" and m.content == "concise answers" for m in memories)
